---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import DataHandling from "../components/DataHandling.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Security · Tracelane"
  description="Security controls, service providers, retention and workspace deletion for Tracelane."
>
  <section class="container-prose prose-page" style="padding-block:clamp(3.5rem,8vw,6.5rem) clamp(5rem,9vw,8.5rem)">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-5">security</p>
    <h1 class="display-lg text-fg">Security posture.</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 lede">
      Tracelane is designed for procurement reviews at regulated buyers. This page describes the service's controls, data handling and deletion boundaries.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-fg">Security controls</h2>
    <ul class="text-fg-muted">
      <li>Workspace authorization and tenant-scoped database queries separate customer data.</li>
      <li>Provider keys use envelope encryption bound to the workspace and provider.</li>
      <li>The gateway origin is configured for TLS 1.3. The public edge and the internal messaging path have different transport boundaries; see the <a href="https://docs.tracelane.dev/security" class="link-accent">security documentation</a>.</li>
      <li>Release controls include Cosign signatures, build provenance and CycloneDX software bills of materials. Dependency and secret scanning are automated checks.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
      The ledger covers gateway-admitted calls and their recorded guardrail verdicts; SDK/OTLP-only spans are captured, not chained; the trace ledger badge shows whether that trace has a ledger record.
      See <a href="https://docs.tracelane.dev/audit-ledger" class="link-accent">ledger coverage and verification</a>.
    </p>

    <DataHandling />

    <h2 class="text-fg">Procurement review</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
      Request the current data-processing terms and supporting security information
      from <a href="mailto:support@tracelane.dev" class="link-accent">support@tracelane.dev</a>.
      The controls and ledger exports described here support your review; they do
      not establish that your application meets a regulatory obligation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-fg">Responsible disclosure</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      Report security issues to <code class="font-mono text-fg">security@tracelane.dev</code>. We acknowledge within 72 hours and target a 30-day patch for critical vulnerabilities.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-16 text-sm text-fg-subtle">Last updated: September 22, 2026.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
